From 025d89e705cb676d7b2df936d7dd1954c667178d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ga=C3=ABl=20Duval?= <gael@murena.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:47:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat(documenteditor): Word-like navigation pane and side
 panels

- No icon rail on the left, like Word: the side panels open on demand
  and the left column takes no room while they are closed.
- Navigation pane (Ctrl+F, View > Navigation): Headings, Pages and
  Results tabs over the headings tree and the search panel. Pages shows
  thumbnails drawn with the print preview renderer; clicking one goes
  to the page. Ctrl+F (Cmd+F) opens Results with the selected text.
- The comments pane docks on the right of the page area, like Word, and
  the pages re-centre in the remaining width; Word-like comment cards.
- Ctrl+wheel and trackpad pinch zoom smoothly (10 % per wheel notch,
  continuous for pinches) instead of jumping between preset steps.
- The properties panel on the right starts closed for new users (View >
  Right panel opens it), like the format panes of Word.
- Title bar: the file name stops before the search box; narrow windows
  show the save state as an icon.

[branding]

Assisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
